      "message": "Dropping `\\0` here makes sense (git fsck rejects NUL in headers). For `\\r`, though, the line-splitting problem only affects reflog lines. Commit and tag headers, `ReflogReaderImpl` and C git all split on LF only, and packed-refs, the example in the commit message, never contains an identity. Since this is shared with `CommitBuilder`/`TagBuilder`, rewriting a C git commit whose author has a CR will now silently change the author. Would it be enough to strip CR from the ident in `ReflogWriter.encode()` and keep `appendSanitized` in line with `strbuf_addstr_without_crud`?",
